Package: displayxr-runtime
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 displayxr-dashboard [amd64],
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin | displayxr-window-geometry-publisher,
 libopenxr-loader1,
Provides:
 libopenxr1,
Description: OpenXR runtime for 3D displays (DisplayXR)
 DisplayXR is an open OpenXR runtime purpose-built for 3D displays, so
 that any OpenXR program runs on a desktop's screens. It is built by
 Sparky Stereo OS from upstream DisplayXR
 (https://github.com/DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime).
 .
 This package ships the runtime library, the displayxr-service compositor
 that a systemd user socket starts on demand, the displayxr-cli tool, and
 the vendor-neutral sim-display display processor used when no vendor
 panel plug-in is installed. In this build sim-display has two outputs:
 2D, and the two views side by side, left first, each at the window's
 resolution, declared to the desktop. Stereo KWin then shows them on every
 stereo display it drives: 3D televisions and projectors, VR headsets,
 glasses-free 3D displays and any monitor with red-cyan glasses, while a
 plain 2D monitor shows the left view unchanged.
 .
 The runtime joins the openxr1-active-runtime alternatives group beside
 other OpenXR runtimes such as Monado; README.Debian says how to choose
 one for the whole system, for one user or for one program.

