Breaks:
 displayxr-runtime (<< 2.66.3-1~),
Replaces:
 displayxr-runtime (<< 2.66.3-1~),
Description: settings and status window for the DisplayXR runtime
 The DisplayXR Dashboard shows the displays, windows, components and
 performance settings of the DisplayXR OpenXR runtime, and changes them,
 through displayxr-cli.
 .
 The dashboard is a self-contained .NET program. Debian has no .NET, so
 this package carries the dashboard of DisplayXR's own release package
 for this version, whose SHA-256 is checked against the digest DisplayXR
 publishes for it; the source package keeps that release file, so what is
 installed can be compared with it.

Package: displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-gnome
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Enhances:
 displayxr-runtime,
 gnome-shell,
Provides:
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher,
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-gnome,
Conflicts:
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-gnome,
Breaks:
 displayxr-runtime (<< 2.66.3-1~),
Replaces:
 displayxr-runtime (<< 2.66.3-1~),
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-gnome,
Description: DisplayXR window-geometry service for GNOME Shell
 A GNOME Shell extension (window-geometry@displayxr.org) that serves
 org.displayxr.WindowGeometry on the session bus: the position and size
 of each window and its monitor, so that the DisplayXR runtime or a
 vendor's runtime can weave a glasses-free panel's picture where the
 window is, and keep its own windows out of screen captures.
 .
 It is enabled once for each user at their next GNOME login, except for a
 user who has turned it off. The KWin service of the same interface is
 displayxr-window-geometry-publisher-kwin.
